# Internal automation / tooling — never serve publicly
.git
.env*
*.py
i18n/
i18n_out/
geo-battery.md
churnlens-site-brand-gap-analysis.csv
pseo-churnlens-site.txt
striking-distance.html
scripts/

# Internal working docs — these were being served 200 and were crawlable. Among
# them QA-SECURITY-SPEED-AUDIT-2026-07-19.md, which enumerates this site's own
# security weaknesses, plus CLAUDE.md (internal ops rules) and the HERMES task /
# report files (unpublished go-to-market strategy). `*.py` and `scripts/` were
# already excluded; `*.md` never was.
#
# NOTE: agents.md and .well-known/agents.md are DELIBERATELY public (AI-agent
# discovery, same role as llms.txt), so this excludes by name rather than *.md.
#
# Globs (not `!` negation) so the families this repo keeps generating are caught
# as they appear, without betting on negation semantics that could silently drop
# agents.md. scripts/check_public_docs.py enforces that nothing new slips past.
CLAUDE.md
HERMES_*.md
REPORT_*.md
OWNER_*.md
*AUDIT*.md
*SCORECARD*.md

# build artifact — 78 duplicate pages, canonicalized to the real URLs, unknown to Google
dist/

# --- agent working files ---
# Preventive. carshake shipped 1,171 files this way on 2026-07-26 — a full
# Claude Code worktree under .claude/, live and indexable on the production
# domain, because the repo root is the deploy root there too. Nothing to
# exclude here today; this is the guard for the day an agent session creates
# one. It is untracked, so `git status` would never show it.
/.claude
